+# host binding, shared by every architecture in ``arches`` -- with the keys
+# ``kernel`` (the kernel symbol ``kernel_<program>``, or the twin's symbol that
+# ``_KERNEL_OVERRIDES`` names for a program whose ``build.json`` entry compiles
+# the twin's kernel source), ``library`` (the program name: the
+# architecture-free stem of its ``build.json`` entries), ``ffi_entry``
+# (``run``), ``arg_plan`` (the binding's positional order as ``[kind, name]``
+# pairs -- ``tma_buffer`` / ``buffer`` tensors, ``parameter`` scalars, the
+# ``launch`` slot ``enable_pdl`` and the trailing grid triple -- one of the
+# shared ``ARG_PLANS``), ``launch`` (block and cluster triples), ``arches``
+# and the stage metadata ``unit``.  A ``_PROGRAMS`` row, keyed by the
+# program's 20-hex digest, holds the stage, the ``ARG_PLANS`` index, the
+# ``_ARG_DTYPES`` index (the storage dtype the binding checks per tensor
+# argument), the ``_TMA_RANKS`` index (the minimum source rank per tensor-map
+# operand) and the block and cluster triples; the stage tables hold the rest
+# of ``unit``:
+#
+# * ``_ROUTING``, per input kind and logits dtype: kind, variant and token
+#   window; ``_ROUTING_KINDS`` gives grid, grid rule, expanded-per-thread
+#   capacity and the cooperative flag of each kind; ``_ROUTING_PRE`` links a
+#   cooperative row to the histogram pre-program launched first (``pre`` on
+#   the cooperative row, ``leads`` on the pre-program);
+# * ``_FC1`` / ``_FC2``: family, tile and K block (FC2 also the block-scale
+#   layout of its activation operand); ``_FAMILY_FACTS`` and ``_GEMM_DTYPES``
+#   give family index, per-token flag, weight layout and operand dtypes;
+# * ``_REQUANT``: variant and block-scale layout; ``_FINALIZE``: variant,
+#   kernel variant, expert-weights dtype and top-k capacity;
+# * ``_STAGE_CONSTANTS``: the ``unit`` fields constant within a stage.
+#
+# ``unit_key`` is ``[stage, family, tile_n]`` for FC1 / FC2 and
+# ``[stage, variant]`` otherwise.  The export's per-program fields
+# ``native_config``, ``num_tokens_static`` and ``threads``
+# (``launch.block[0]``) are not carried: nothing in the package or its tests
+# reads them.
+#
+# ``STAGE_TABLES``: the five dispatch tables of the pipeline (``routing``,
+# ``fc1``, ``requant``, ``fc2``, ``finalize``) as ordered program-name lists;
+# every row fact lives once, in ``PROGRAMS[name]["unit"]``.  The routing table
+# is in dispatcher order (per input kind and logits dtype, ascending token
+# windows); the two histogram pre-programs of the cooperative rows are reached
+# through ``unit["pre"]`` only.
+#
+# ``HOST_PLAN_CONSTANTS``: the geometry, family, routing, requantization and
+# finalize constants the package backend's host plan evaluates.
+#
+# The export's measurement catalogue -- ``ROUTES``, one record per measured
+# route (per-stage units and the full routing -> FC1 -> [requant] -> FC2 ->
+# finalize path per family and tile) naming its architectures, token count
+# and ordered stages -- is not part of the runtime registry; it lives with the
+# tests as ``tests/test_helpers/cake_stepfun_moe_routes.json``.
+#
+# What to compile (the translation units, the compile flags and the per-entry
+# closure digest) is recorded in ``build.json`` (see ``cake_build``), whose
+# entry for a program is ``<library>_<arch>``; a program is built once per
+# architecture, prebuilt under ``aot/`` or by FlashInfer's JIT.  An entry's
+# ``closure_sha256`` -- the salt of its JIT library name -- is the SHA-256 over
+# the length-framed items [entry name, architecture, each nvcc flag, then each
+# source's package-relative path and its bytes], every item prefixed by its
+# byte length as eight little-endian bytes; a changed source, flag or source
+# set therefore names a fresh build.
